{
  "id": "29401_toritsuku",
  "headword": "{取|と}り{付|つ}く",
  "reading": "とりつく",
  "romaji": "toritsuku",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to cling to; to grab hold of",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to cling to; to grab hold of",
      "explanation": "To cling or catch hold of something or someone. By extension it can mean to set to work on a task (X に {取|と}り{付|つ}く); the thing clung to or tackled is marked with に."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29401_toritsuku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもが{母親|ははおや}に{取|と}り{付|つ}く。",
      "english": "The child clings to its mother.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29401_toritsuku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{難|むずか}しい{問題|もんだい}に{取|と}り{付|つ}く。",
      "english": "to tackle a difficult problem",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29401_toritsuku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{冷|つめ}たくて、{取|と}り{付|つ}く{島|しま}もなかった。",
      "english": "He was so cold that there was no way to approach him.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). The thing clung to or tackled is marked with に.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {取|と}り{付|つ}く{島|しま}もない: to be utterly unapproachable; to leave one no opening (literally \"not even an island to cling to\")\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {取|と}り{憑|つ}く: to possess (of a spirit) — same reading, written with {憑|つ}く; a ghost or obsession takes hold of someone\n- しがみつく: to cling tightly — more physical and desperate",
